= Let's Encrypt moving to 64-day certificate lifetimes in
2027
[Security] Posted Oct 9, 2026 14:02 UTC (Fri) by jzb
[68]Let's Encrypt, the nonprofit that provides free TLS
certificates for millions of sites, has [69]announced that
it will be moving to certificates with 64-day lifetimes on
February 10, 2027:
This means that any certificate we issue or renew on and
after that date will have a 64 day validity period, and we
expect the last 90-day certificate to expire on May 11,
2027. We will not revoke valid certificates as a part of
this process.
This is the second stage of Let's Encrypt's plan,
[70]announced in 2025, to move to 45-day certificate
lifetimes as required by the the [71]CA/Browser Forum
Baseline Requirements. In 2028, Let's Encrypt will switch
to 45-day certificates.
