= OpenSSH 10.6 released
[Security] Posted Oct 6, 2026 13:42 UTC (Tue) by jzb
[82]Version 10.6 of OpenSSH has been released. The
announcement notes that the OpenSSH team has been
receiving a large number of AI-assisted security bug
reports. "We very much welcome these reports, especially
when combined with human triage, analysis, test-cases and
particularly when accompanied by proposed fixes". As a
result, the project expects to be making more frequent
releases to get updates to users more quickly rather than
batching the bug fixes until the next planned release.
Notable changes in this release include enabling the
hybrid post-quantum ssh-mldsa44-ed25519 signature
algorithm, addition of a -p option for [83]sftp's
[84]lmkdir/[85]mkdir commands, as well as disabling the
LZ77 dictionary coder in [86]ssh and [87]sshd to mitigate
side-channel leaks (which will result in reduced
effectiveness of the Compression option). The [88]scp -R
option, which allows copies between two remote hosts, is
being deprecated due to security risks; the option will be
ignored in the future. See the announcement for full
details of all changes and bug fixes.
